{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getSize"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getSize: () => number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the current size of the column"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getstart","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getStart"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getStart: (position?: ColumnPinningPosition) => number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the offset measurement along the row-axis (usually the x-axis for standard tables) for the column, measuring the size of all preceding columns."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Useful for sticky or absolute positioning of columns. (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"left"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transform"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getafter","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getAfter"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getAfter: (position?: ColumnPinningPosition) => number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the offset measurement along the row-axis (usually the x-axis for standard tables) for the column, measuring the size of all succeeding columns."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Useful for sticky or absolute positioning of columns. (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"right"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transform"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getcanresize","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCanResize"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getCanResize: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" if the column can be resized."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getisresizing","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsResizing"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getIsResizing: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" if the column is currently being resized."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"resetsize","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resetSize"}]},{"type":"code","value":"resetSize: () => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resets the column size to its initial size."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"header-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Header API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getsize-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getSize"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getSize: () => number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the size for the header, calculated by summing the size of all leaf-columns that belong to it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getstart-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getStart"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getStart: (position?: ColumnPinningPosition) => number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the offset measurement along the row-axis (usually the x-axis for standard tables) for the header. This is effectively a sum of the offset measurements of all preceding headers."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getresizehandler","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getResizeHandler"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getResizeHandler: () => (event: unknown) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns an event handler function that can be used to resize the header. It can be used as an:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onMouseDown"},{"type":"text","value":" handler"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onTouchStart"},{"type":"text","value":" handler"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The dragging and release events are automatically handled for you."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"table-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enablecolumnresizing","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableColumnResizing"}]},{"type":"code","value":"enableColumnResizing?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables/disables column resizing for *all columns**."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"columnresizemode","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnResizeMode"}]},{"type":"code","value":"columnResizeMode?: 'onChange' | 'onEnd'","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Determines when the columnSizing state is updated. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChange"},{"type":"text","value":" updates the state when the user is dragging the resize handle. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onEnd"},{"type":"text","value":" updates the state when the user releases the resize handle."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"columnresizedirection","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnResizeDirection"}]},{"type":"code","value":"columnResizeDirection?: 'ltr' | 'rtl'","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables or disables right-to-left support for resizing the column. defaults to 'ltr'."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"oncolumnsizingchange","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onColumnSizingChange"}]},{"type":"code","value":"onColumnSizingChange?: OnChangeFn<ColumnSizingState>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This optional function will be called when the columnSizing state changes. If you provide this function, you will be responsible for maintaining its state yourself. You can pass this state back to the table via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.columnSizing"},{"type":"text","value":" table option."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"oncolumnsizinginfochange","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onColumnSizingInfoChange"}]},{"type":"code","value":"onColumnSizingInfoChange?: OnChangeFn<ColumnSizingInfoState>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This optional function will be called when the columnSizingInfo state changes. If you provide this function, you will be responsible for maintaining its state yourself. You can pass this state back to the table via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.columnSizingInfo"},{"type":"text","value":" table option."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"table-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"setcolumnsizing","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setColumnSizing"}]},{"type":"code","value":"setColumnSizing: (updater: Updater<ColumnSizingState>) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sets the column sizing state using an updater function or a value. This will trigger the underlying "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onColumnSizingChange"},{"type":"text","value":" function if one is passed to the table options, otherwise the state will be managed automatically by the table."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"setcolumnsizinginfo","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setColumnSizingInfo"}]},{"type":"code","value":"setColumnSizingInfo: (updater: Updater<ColumnSizingInfoState>) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sets the column sizing info state using an updater function or a value. This will trigger the underlying "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onColumnSizingInfoChange"},{"type":"text","value":" function if one is passed to the table options, otherwise the state will be managed automatically by the table."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"resetcolumnsizing","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resetColumnSizing"}]},{"type":"code","value":"resetColumnSizing: (defaultState?: boolean) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resets column sizing to its initial state. If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultState"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", the default state for the table will be used instead of the initialValue provided to the table."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"resetheadersizeinfo","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resetHeaderSizeInfo"}]},{"type":"code","value":"resetHeaderSizeInfo: (defaultState?: boolean) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resets column sizing info to its initial state. If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultState"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", the default state for the table will be used instead of the initialValue provided to the table."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"gettotalsize","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getTotalSize"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getTotalSize: () => number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the total size of the table by calculating the sum of the sizes of all leaf-columns."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getlefttotalsize","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getLeftTotalSize"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getLeftTotalSize: () => number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If pinning, returns the total size of the left portion of the table by calculating the sum of the sizes of all left leaf-columns."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getcentertotalsize","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCenterTotalSize"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getCenterTotalSize: () => number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If pinning, returns the total size of the center portion of the table by calculating the sum of the sizes of all unpinned/center leaf-columns."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getrighttotalsize","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getRightTotalSize"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getRightTotalSize: () => number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If pinning, returns the total size of the right portion of the table by calculating the sum of the sizes of all right leaf-columns."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"state","text":"State","level":2},{"id":"column-def-options","text":"Column Def Options","level":2},{"id":"enableresizing","text":"enableResizing","level":3},{"id":"size","text":"size","level":3},{"id":"minsize","text":"minSize","level":3},{"id":"maxsize","text":"maxSize","level":3},{"id":"column-api","text":"Column API","level":2},{"id":"getsize","text":"getSize","level":3},{"id":"getstart","text":"getStart","level":3},{"id":"getafter","text":"getAfter","level":3},{"id":"getcanresize","text":"getCanResize","level":3},{"id":"getisresizing","text":"getIsResizing","level":3},{"id":"resetsize","text":"resetSize","level":3},{"id":"header-api","text":"Header API","level":2},{"id":"getsize-2","text":"getSize","level":3},{"id":"getstart-2","text":"getStart","level":3},{"id":"getresizehandler","text":"getResizeHandler","level":3},{"id":"table-options","text":"Table Options","level":2},{"id":"enablecolumnresizing","text":"enableColumnResizing","level":3},{"id":"columnresizemode","text":"columnResizeMode","level":3},{"id":"columnresizedirection","text":"columnResizeDirection","level":3},{"id":"oncolumnsizingchange","text":"onColumnSizingChange","level":3},{"id":"oncolumnsizinginfochange","text":"onColumnSizingInfoChange","level":3},{"id":"table-api","text":"Table API","level":2},{"id":"setcolumnsizing","text":"setColumnSizing","level":3},{"id":"setcolumnsizinginfo","text":"setColumnSizingInfo","level":3},{"id":"resetcolumnsizing","text":"resetColumnSizing","level":3},{"id":"resetheadersizeinfo","text":"resetHeaderSizeInfo","level":3},{"id":"gettotalsize","text":"getTotalSize","level":3},{"id":"getlefttotalsize","text":"getLeftTotalSize","level":3},{"id":"getcentertotalsize","text":"getCenterTotalSize","level":3},{"id":"getrighttotalsize","text":"getRightTotalSize","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## State\n\nColumn sizing state is stored on the table using the following shape:\n\n```tsx\nexport type ColumnSizingTableState = {\n  columnSizing: ColumnSizing\n  columnSizingInfo: ColumnSizingInfoState\n}\n\nexport type ColumnSizing = Record<string, number>\n\nexport type ColumnSizingInfoState = {\n  startOffset: null | number\n  startSize: null | number\n  deltaOffset: null | number\n  deltaPercentage: null | number\n  isResizingColumn: false | string\n  columnSizingStart: [string, number][]\n}\n```\n\n## Column Def Options\n\n### `enableResizing`\n\n```tsx\nenableResizing?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables or disables column resizing for the column.\n\n### `size`\n\n```tsx\nsize?: number\n```\n\nThe desired size for the column\n\n### `minSize`\n\n```tsx\nminSize?: number\n```\n\nThe minimum allowed size for the column\n\n### `maxSize`\n\n```tsx\nmaxSize?: number\n```\n\nThe maximum allowed size for the column\n\n## Column API\n\n### `getSize`\n\n```tsx\ngetSize: () => number\n```\n\nReturns the current size of the column\n\n### `getStart`\n\n```tsx\ngetStart: (position?: ColumnPinningPosition) => number\n```\n\nReturns the offset measurement along the row-axis (usually the x-axis for standard tables) for the column, measuring the size of all preceding columns.\n\nUseful for sticky or absolute positioning of columns. (e.g. `left` or `transform`)\n\n### `getAfter`\n\n```tsx\ngetAfter: (position?: ColumnPinningPosition) => number\n```\n\nReturns the offset measurement along the row-axis (usually the x-axis for standard tables) for the column, measuring the size of all succeeding columns.\n\nUseful for sticky or absolute positioning of columns. (e.g. `right` or `transform`)\n\n### `getCanResize`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanResize: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns `true` if the column can be resized.\n\n### `getIsResizing`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsResizing: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns `true` if the column is currently being resized.\n\n### `resetSize`\n\n```tsx\nresetSize: () => void\n```\n\nResets the column size to its initial size.\n\n## Header API\n\n### `getSize`\n\n```tsx\ngetSize: () => number\n```\n\nReturns the size for the header, calculated by summing the size of all leaf-columns that belong to it.\n\n### `getStart`\n\n```tsx\ngetStart: (position?: ColumnPinningPosition) => number\n```\n\nReturns the offset measurement along the row-axis (usually the x-axis for standard tables) for the header. This is effectively a sum of the offset measurements of all preceding headers.\n\n### `getResizeHandler`\n\n```tsx\ngetResizeHandler: () => (event: unknown) => void\n```\n\nReturns an event handler function that can be used to resize the header. It can be used as an:\n\n- `onMouseDown` handler\n- `onTouchStart` handler\n\nThe dragging and release events are automatically handled for you.\n\n## Table Options\n\n### `enableColumnResizing`\n\n```tsx\nenableColumnResizing?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/disables column resizing for \\*all columns\\*\\*.\n\n### `columnResizeMode`\n\n```tsx\ncolumnResizeMode?: 'onChange' | 'onEnd'\n```\n\nDetermines when the columnSizing state is updated. `onChange` updates the state when the user is dragging the resize handle. `onEnd` updates the state when the user releases the resize handle.\n\n### `columnResizeDirection`\n\n```tsx\ncolumnResizeDirection?: 'ltr' | 'rtl'\n```\n\nEnables or disables right-to-left support for resizing the column. defaults to 'ltr'.\n\n### `onColumnSizingChange`\n\n```tsx\nonColumnSizingChange?: OnChangeFn<ColumnSizingState>\n```\n\nThis optional function will be called when the columnSizing state changes. If you provide this function, you will be responsible for maintaining its state yourself. You can pass this state back to the table via the `state.columnSizing` table option.\n\n### `onColumnSizingInfoChange`\n\n```tsx\nonColumnSizingInfoChange?: OnChangeFn<ColumnSizingInfoState>\n```\n\nThis optional function will be called when the columnSizingInfo state changes. If you provide this function, you will be responsible for maintaining its state yourself. You can pass this state back to the table via the `state.columnSizingInfo` table option.\n\n## Table API\n\n### `setColumnSizing`\n\n```tsx\nsetColumnSizing: (updater: Updater<ColumnSizingState>) => void\n```\n\nSets the column sizing state using an updater function or a value. This will trigger the underlying `onColumnSizingChange` function if one is passed to the table options, otherwise the state will be managed automatically by the table.\n\n### `setColumnSizingInfo`\n\n```tsx\nsetColumnSizingInfo: (updater: Updater<ColumnSizingInfoState>) => void\n```\n\nSets the column sizing info state using an updater function or a value. This will trigger the underlying `onColumnSizingInfoChange` function if one is passed to the table options, otherwise the state will be managed automatically by the table.\n\n### `resetColumnSizing`\n\n```tsx\nresetColumnSizing: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nResets column sizing to its initial state. If `defaultState` is `true`, the default state for the table will be used instead of the initialValue provided to the table.\n\n### `resetHeaderSizeInfo`\n\n```tsx\nresetHeaderSizeInfo: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nResets column sizing info to its initial state. If `defaultState` is `true`, the default state for the table will be used instead of the initialValue provided to the table.\n\n### `getTotalSize`\n\n```tsx\ngetTotalSize: () => number\n```\n\nReturns the total size of the table by calculating the sum of the sizes of all leaf-columns.\n\n### `getLeftTotalSize`\n\n```tsx\ngetLeftTotalSize: () => number\n```\n\nIf pinning, returns the total size of the left portion of the table by calculating the sum of the sizes of all left leaf-columns.\n\n### `getCenterTotalSize`\n\n```tsx\ngetCenterTotalSize: () => number\n```\n\nIf pinning, returns the total size of the center portion of the table by calculating the sum of the sizes of all unpinned/center leaf-columns.\n\n### `getRightTotalSize`\n\n```tsx\ngetRightTotalSize: () => number\n```\n\nIf pinning, returns the total size of the right portion of the table by calculating the sum of the sizes of all right leaf-columns.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Column Sizing APIs\nid: column-sizing\n---\n\n## State\n\nColumn sizing state is stored on the table using the following shape:\n\n```tsx\nexport type ColumnSizingTableState = {\n  columnSizing: ColumnSizing\n  columnSizingInfo: ColumnSizingInfoState\n}\n\nexport type ColumnSizing = Record<string, number>\n\nexport type ColumnSizingInfoState = {\n  startOffset: null | number\n  startSize: null | number\n  deltaOffset: null | number\n  deltaPercentage: null | number\n  isResizingColumn: false | string\n  columnSizingStart: [string, number][]\n}\n```\n\n## Column Def Options\n\n### `enableResizing`\n\n```tsx\nenableResizing?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables or disables column resizing for the column.\n\n### `size`\n\n```tsx\nsize?: number\n```\n\nThe desired size for the column\n\n### `minSize`\n\n```tsx\nminSize?: number\n```\n\nThe minimum allowed size for the column\n\n### `maxSize`\n\n```tsx\nmaxSize?: number\n```\n\nThe maximum allowed size for the column\n\n## Column API\n\n### `getSize`\n\n```tsx\ngetSize: () => number\n```\n\nReturns the current size of the column\n\n### `getStart`\n\n```tsx\ngetStart: (position?: ColumnPinningPosition) => number\n```\n\nReturns the offset measurement along the row-axis (usually the x-axis for standard tables) for the column, measuring the size of all preceding columns.\n\nUseful for sticky or absolute positioning of columns. (e.g. `left` or `transform`)\n\n### `getAfter`\n\n```tsx\ngetAfter: (position?: ColumnPinningPosition) => number\n```\n\nReturns the offset measurement along the row-axis (usually the x-axis for standard tables) for the column, measuring the size of all succeeding columns.\n\nUseful for sticky or absolute positioning of columns. (e.g. `right` or `transform`)\n\n### `getCanResize`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanResize: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns `true` if the column can be resized.\n\n### `getIsResizing`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsResizing: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns `true` if the column is currently being resized.\n\n### `resetSize`\n\n```tsx\nresetSize: () => void\n```\n\nResets the column size to its initial size.\n\n## Header API\n\n### `getSize`\n\n```tsx\ngetSize: () => number\n```\n\nReturns the size for the header, calculated by summing the size of all leaf-columns that belong to it.\n\n### `getStart`\n\n```tsx\ngetStart: (position?: ColumnPinningPosition) => number\n```\n\nReturns the offset measurement along the row-axis (usually the x-axis for standard tables) for the header. This is effectively a sum of the offset measurements of all preceding headers.\n\n### `getResizeHandler`\n\n```tsx\ngetResizeHandler: () => (event: unknown) => void\n```\n\nReturns an event handler function that can be used to resize the header. It can be used as an:\n\n- `onMouseDown` handler\n- `onTouchStart` handler\n\nThe dragging and release events are automatically handled for you.\n\n## Table Options\n\n### `enableColumnResizing`\n\n```tsx\nenableColumnResizing?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables/disables column resizing for \\*all columns\\*\\*.\n\n### `columnResizeMode`\n\n```tsx\ncolumnResizeMode?: 'onChange' | 'onEnd'\n```\n\nDetermines when the columnSizing state is updated. `onChange` updates the state when the user is dragging the resize handle. `onEnd` updates the state when the user releases the resize handle.\n\n### `columnResizeDirection`\n\n```tsx\ncolumnResizeDirection?: 'ltr' | 'rtl'\n```\n\nEnables or disables right-to-left support for resizing the column. defaults to 'ltr'.\n\n### `onColumnSizingChange`\n\n```tsx\nonColumnSizingChange?: OnChangeFn<ColumnSizingState>\n```\n\nThis optional function will be called when the columnSizing state changes. If you provide this function, you will be responsible for maintaining its state yourself. You can pass this state back to the table via the `state.columnSizing` table option.\n\n### `onColumnSizingInfoChange`\n\n```tsx\nonColumnSizingInfoChange?: OnChangeFn<ColumnSizingInfoState>\n```\n\nThis optional function will be called when the columnSizingInfo state changes. If you provide this function, you will be responsible for maintaining its state yourself. You can pass this state back to the table via the `state.columnSizingInfo` table option.\n\n## Table API\n\n### `setColumnSizing`\n\n```tsx\nsetColumnSizing: (updater: Updater<ColumnSizingState>) => void\n```\n\nSets the column sizing state using an updater function or a value. This will trigger the underlying `onColumnSizingChange` function if one is passed to the table options, otherwise the state will be managed automatically by the table.\n\n### `setColumnSizingInfo`\n\n```tsx\nsetColumnSizingInfo: (updater: Updater<ColumnSizingInfoState>) => void\n```\n\nSets the column sizing info state using an updater function or a value. This will trigger the underlying `onColumnSizingInfoChange` function if one is passed to the table options, otherwise the state will be managed automatically by the table.\n\n### `resetColumnSizing`\n\n```tsx\nresetColumnSizing: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nResets column sizing to its initial state. If `defaultState` is `true`, the default state for the table will be used instead of the initialValue provided to the table.\n\n### `resetHeaderSizeInfo`\n\n```tsx\nresetHeaderSizeInfo: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nResets column sizing info to its initial state. If `defaultState` is `true`, the default state for the table will be used instead of the initialValue provided to the table.\n\n### `getTotalSize`\n\n```tsx\ngetTotalSize: () => number\n```\n\nReturns the total size of the table by calculating the sum of the sizes of all leaf-columns.\n\n### `getLeftTotalSize`\n\n```tsx\ngetLeftTotalSize: () => number\n```\n\nIf pinning, returns the total size of the left portion of the table by calculating the sum of the sizes of all left leaf-columns.\n\n### `getCenterTotalSize`\n\n```tsx\ngetCenterTotalSize: () => number\n```\n\nIf pinning, returns the total size of the center portion of the table by calculating the sum of the sizes of all unpinned/center leaf-columns.\n\n### `getRightTotalSize`\n\n```tsx\ngetRightTotalSize: () => number\n```\n\nIf pinning, returns the total size of the right portion of the table by calculating the sum of the sizes of all right leaf-columns.\n"}
